course: dictionary
lesson: 4739
title: Horrid: nasty, mean or frightening
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Horrid is a word you will meet often in children's books and in everyday talk. The context tells you which meaning it has. «A horrid smell» means something very unpleasant, the kind of smell that makes you hold your nose.
explain: Ask whether the word describes a thing or a person. «Don't be horrid to your sister» is about how someone treats another person, so horrid means unkind or mean. The sentence around the word is your clue.
explain: Horrid can also mean causing horror or frightening, but this is an old use that you will see mostly in older writing. When you meet horrid, swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Horrid means very unpleasant or nasty, as in «a horrid smell».
fact: Horrid can describe a person who is unkind or mean, as in «Don't be horrid to your sister».
fact: In older writing, horrid can mean frightening or causing horror.
fact: «Horrid Henry» is a famous naughty character in children's books.
fact: Horrid is an adjective. Its comparative and superlative forms are more horrid and most horrid, or the older horrider and horridest.
exercise: «A horrid smell» filled the kitchen. What does horrid mean here? | Very shiny and new | Very kind and gentle | *Very unpleasant or nasty | Very quiet and calm
exercise: «Don't be horrid to your sister.» What does horrid mean here? | Very tall | *Unkind or mean | Very tasty | Happy to play
exercise: A field-mouse says the machines are horrid, because the mice «must move before those horrid machines begin clicking round the fields». Why might the mice dislike them? | The machines are very small | The machines are made of paper | The machines are sweet and cuddly | *The machines will make the mice have to move from their home
test: Lily says, «Don't be horrid!» What does she mean? | *You are being unkind | You are being very clever | You are being very quiet | You are being very late
test: In an old tale, a «horrid» storm fills the villagers with dread. What does horrid mean here? | *Frightening, causing horror | Kind and helpful | Wet and grey | Tasty and sweet
exam: Which meaning of horrid fits «a horrid smell»? | *Very unpleasant or nasty | Very happy and cheerful | Causing horror in an old story | Unkind or mean to a friend
